# A spec with a second YAML document gets SV000 at the line of that document.
# speclint reads only the first document, so it must not pass the spec.
exits 1 slint check specs/two.yaml
cmp stdout two.txt

-- .speclint.yaml --
-- .speclint/data/services.yaml --
services:
  OrderManager: { layer: manager }
  OrderAccessor: { layer: accessor }
-- specs/two.yaml --
speclint: 1
id: A-1
kind: chore
title: T
summary: S
acceptance: [{ id: AC1, text: "Given an order, when it is read, then it is returned." }]
calls: [{ from: OrderManager, to: OrderAccessor, op: Get, covers: [AC1] }]
---
calls: [{ from: OrderAccessor, to: OrderManager, op: Get, covers: [AC1] }]
-- two.txt --
specs/two.yaml:8 error SV000 The spec has more than one YAML document. speclint reads only the first.
    fix: Remove the line with three dashes and the document after it. Put each spec in its own file.
specs/two.yaml note: The other rules run after you fix the format errors (SV000, SV001).
speclint checked 1 spec(s) and found 1 error(s) and 0 warning(s).
